From: NWP ops#139 (R1.4 part 2a)
Subject: [PATCH] depthcontent: anchor every course module to its canonical pointid

ops#139 / REMEDIATION-PLAN R1.4 part 2. The Moodle course-module NAME is the
doctrine title (populate_courses.php:187), and core stamps that name into
logstore_standard_log.other['name'] on course_module_created/updated — a
mandatory core field (lib/classes/event/course_module_created.php:126-128), so
it cannot be dropped at the event level.

This patch does NOT change the displayed name. It fills the course-module
idnumber slot, which populate_courses.php sets to '' and nothing else uses,
with the canonical learning-point id (e.g. B5.03).

Why that is worth doing on its own:

  * Every log row for these modules gains a canonical anchor reachable by a
    join that does NOT pass through the doctrine title.
  * It is a prerequisite for the real declassification (option A in
    docs/guides/ops139-logstore-declassification.md §2b — making the cm name
    itself opaque), which is a member-facing display change and an OPERATOR
    decision this patch deliberately does not take.
  * It is additive: no DB schema change, no display change, no behaviour
    change for members. course_modules.idnumber is currently empty for every
    depthcontent module.

Applies to mod/depthcontent in the ss-moodle-plugins canonical repo. The
patch must also land in (or be re-synced to) the ssd checkout, which carries
the same plugin.

--- a/mod/depthcontent/cli/populate_courses.php
+++ b/mod/depthcontent/cli/populate_courses.php
@@ -191,8 +191,13 @@
         $moduleinfo->pointid = $pointid;
         $moduleinfo->content_json = $json;

         // Required fields for add_moduleinfo().
-        $moduleinfo->cmidnumber = '';
+        // ops#139: anchor the course module to its CANONICAL learning-point id
+        // (e.g. B5.03) rather than leaving the slot empty. The doctrine title
+        // still populates ->name, so nothing member-facing changes here; this
+        // gives every logstore row a canonical join target that does not pass
+        // through the title. See docs/guides/ops139-logstore-declassification.md.
+        $moduleinfo->cmidnumber = $pointid;
         $moduleinfo->groupmode = 0;
         $moduleinfo->groupingid = 0;
         $moduleinfo->showdescription = 0;
